    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d481">

                <pb facs="0839" n="1797" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1797"/>

                <head>No. 26.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Sir L. S. Sackville
                            West</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-10-13"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 13,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge your note
                    of yesterday, in relation to the cases of seizure of the British schooners <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Onward, Carolena</hi>, and <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Thornton</hi>, in Behring Sea, by United States revenue vessels, in August,
                    1886, and also your instructions to include by similar representations the cases
                    of the British Columbian vessels <hi rendition="#italic">Grace, Dolphin</hi>,
                    and <hi rendition="#italic">W. P. Sayward</hi>, seized by the United States
                    revenue authorities in Behring Sea, with notification that Her Britannic
                    Majesty’s Government reserves all right to compensation on behalf of the owners
                    and crews of the above-mentioned vessels. The affidavit of the mate of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">W. P. Sayward</hi> has been read, and the facts therein
                    stated will be at once investigated.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
